### scripts/exp_rlcd_loo_transfer.py
1: """EXP-RLCD-LOO — leave-one-family-out transfer of fine-tuned Laya (2026-09-27).
2: 
3: Journal-level RQ2 evidence for the fine-tuning line: can a Laya System-1
4: fine-tuned (RLCD proper-score / BT pairs) on FOUR families transfer to an
5: unseen fifth, at the decision level?
6: 
7: Design: 5 folds. Each fold trains both arms on the other four families
8: (early stopping on a held-out seed slice OF THE TRAIN FAMILIES) and
9: evaluates on all records of the held-out family: pairwise accuracy,
10: top-1 agreement, mean log score vs that family's teacher labels. The RF
11: baseline is retrained per fold on raw rollout utilities (decision-level
12: metrics are invariant to per-record monotone utility transforms, so no
13: cross-family scale pooling is needed).
14: 
15: Runs fold-tasks as spawned GPU worker processes (two by default).
16: 
17: Usage:
18:     .venv/bin/python scripts/exp_rlcd_loo_transfer.py --workers 2
19: """
20: 
